new file mode 100644
index 0000000..25d8364
--- /dev/null
+++ b/files/research.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# Live compatibility research
+
+Consulted on 2026-08-14 UTC using live network fetches.
+
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation 5.1.1 Release Notes** — https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-5-2-and-earlier/5-1/vcf-release-notes/vmware-cloud-foundation-511-release-notes.html — established the source BOM: SDDC Manager 5.1.1, vCenter 8.0 Update 2b, ESXi 8.0 Update 2b, vSAN Witness 8.0 Update 2, and NSX 4.1.2.3.
+- **Upgrade the Management Domain to VMware Cloud Foundation 5.2.x** — https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-5-2-and-earlier/5-2/vmware-cloud-foundation-lifecycle-management/upgrade-the-management-domain-to-vmware-cloud-foundation-5-2-lifecycle.html — established the management-domain precheck and component order: SDDC Manager, NSX, vCenter, then ESXi; the pinned stretched-cluster sequence refines that order by placing the witness before the hosts.
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation 5.2.3 Release Notes** — https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-5-2-and-earlier/5-2/vcf-release-notes/vmware-cloud-foundation-523-release-notes.html — established the intermediate BOM used in the plan and its 24 February 2026 release date, preserving the forward-only move to 9.1.
+- **Upgrading to VMware Cloud Foundation 9.1** — https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-1/deployment/upgrading-cloud-foundation.html — established that versions earlier than 5.2 must first reach 5.2.x, that 5.2.x supports a skip-level upgrade to 9.1, and the strict 9.1 component order including witness before ESX.
+- **Bill of Materials** — https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-1/release-notes/vmware-cloud-foundation-9-1-0-0-release-notes/vmware-cloud-foundation-bill-of-materials.html — established the 9.1.0.0 target versions for VCF Installer/SDDC Manager, vCenter, ESX, vSAN OSA Witness, and NSX.
+- **Product Interoperability Matrix** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Upgrade?productId=851 — cross-checked the Cloud Foundation upgrade-path and interoperability surface linked by Broadcom's release and lifecycle documentation.
